# Golf Masters agent brief

Treat `Golf-Masters-PRD.md` as the product source of truth.

Current priority: Menu/UI first, followed by the playable solo course shell.

Technical direction:
- Three.js/WebGL renders the course and decorative menu scene.
- Matter.js owns browser-side ball and obstacle physics.
- The whole course, ball, and cup must remain visible on portrait mobile screens.
- Desktop and touch controls must share the same drag-to-aim interaction.
- Keep active match questions visible for the full answering period.
- Use the core blue, green, and red palette with accessible contrast.
- Sound effects must respect the saved sound preference.

Before shipping, run the automated tests, production build, and rendered desktop/mobile browser checks.
